WEBVTT

00:00:05.867 --> 00:00:09.267
Yeah, so, uh, I'm gonna head back
to the training center.

00:00:09.947 --> 00:00:12.107
I think we both know it's for the best.

00:00:15.707 --> 00:00:17.427
But can I ask you something?

00:00:20.067 --> 00:00:22.027
What was it like for you?

00:00:22.107 --> 00:00:24.067
When you showed up to your first race?

00:00:25.427 --> 00:00:27.027
How did you know you could do it?

00:00:29.067 --> 00:00:32.347
I don't know.
I just never thought I couldn't.

00:00:36.347 --> 00:00:38.347
I wish I knew what that felt like.

00:00:41.027 --> 00:00:42.667
Good luck, Mr. McQueen.

00:00:44.107 --> 00:00:47.067
Cruz. Cruz, wait.

00:00:48.827 --> 00:00:50.227
(SIGHS)

00:00:51.027 --> 00:00:52.627
FEMALE CAR ON TV:
And earn your physics degree

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:54.067
from the comfort of your own home--

00:00:54.227 --> 00:00:55.947
MALE CAR: You'll get
that and a $200 gift,

00:00:55.987 --> 00:00:57.507
-for $29.95.
-(MACK SNORING)

00:00:57.667 --> 00:00:58.827
MALE CAR 2: Now look here, Warden...

00:00:58.867 --> 00:00:59.987
FEMALE CAR 2: Oh, no!
He's got a jack!

00:01:01.547 --> 00:01:03.307
NARRATOR: Autos over 100,000 miles
also reported trouble sleeping.

00:01:03.467 --> 00:01:06.907
You could have 12 worn-out wrenches
or you could have one atomic wrench.

00:01:07.067 --> 00:01:08.667
MALE CAR: Throw the old ones out.
This covers--

00:01:08.827 --> 00:01:10.827
HICKS: "Champion for the Ages"
Chick Hicks here.

00:01:11.067 --> 00:01:13.187
Coming to you live from...
Chick Hicks Studios,

00:01:13.267 --> 00:01:14.387
where I'm joined once again by...

00:01:14.547 --> 00:01:16.507
next-gen racing expert, Natalie Certain.

00:01:16.907 --> 00:01:21.227
Thanks, Chick. Piston Cup champion
Jackson Storm set a new record today...

00:01:21.387 --> 00:01:24.027
when he pulled off
the fastest lap ever recorded.

00:01:24.187 --> 00:01:27.947
An unprecedented 213 miles an hour.

00:01:28.747 --> 00:01:30.667
HICKS: Wow!
So what do you think, Certain?

00:01:30.827 --> 00:01:33.307
Stormy boy gonna start
the season with another win?

00:01:33.467 --> 00:01:34.587
Highly likely, Chick.

00:01:34.667 --> 00:01:36.987
Based on his recent run times
and forecasted...

00:01:37.147 --> 00:01:38.347
track temperatures on race day,

00:01:38.467 --> 00:01:42.027
Storm's chances of winning...
are 95.2%.

00:01:42.507 --> 00:01:43.507
That low, huh?

00:01:43.587 --> 00:01:45.787
Oh, and in case you missed it,

00:01:45.867 --> 00:01:47.627
talk of the track tonight
is Lightning McQueen...

00:01:47.787 --> 00:01:50.667
finding yet another way
to embarrass himself

00:01:50.707 --> 00:01:52.347
at a demolition derby. Whoa.

00:01:53.427 --> 00:01:54.827
Almost makes me feel sorry for the guy.

00:01:54.867 --> 00:01:55.867
Not really. (CHUCKLES)

00:01:56.547 --> 00:01:57.787
Here's what his new sponsor had to say.

00:01:58.267 --> 00:02:00.547
Everyone, relax. The 95's gonna race.

00:02:00.707 --> 00:02:04.427
Lightning's just taking a somewhat
unconventional approach to this race.

00:02:04.587 --> 00:02:05.987
It's one of the things
his fans love about him.

00:02:07.227 --> 00:02:09.187
HICKS: Yeah, right!
Talk about humiliating.

00:02:09.427 --> 00:02:10.547
If I were old Ka-chow...
I wouldn't even bother

00:02:10.747 --> 00:02:12.707
to show up in Florida.

00:02:12.867 --> 00:02:15.187
That could be for the best, Chick.
Even if he does race...

00:02:15.827 --> 00:02:19.387
McQueen's probability
of winning is 1.2%.

00:02:19.467 --> 00:02:20.467
HICKS: Wow!

00:02:20.867 --> 00:02:22.987
Numbers never lie.

00:02:23.147 --> 00:02:25.787
I'm willing to predict tonight
that Lightning McQueen's racing...

00:02:25.947 --> 00:02:29.307
career will be over within the week.

00:02:29.387 --> 00:02:30.827
It might even be over now.

00:02:30.947 --> 00:02:32.867
I mean, I knew his career
was stuck in the mud--

00:02:34.747 --> 00:02:35.947
(SIGHS)

00:02:37.107 --> 00:02:38.987
♪ First you find a can from a rusty van

00:02:39.107 --> 00:02:40.107
♪ Bump-bump

00:02:40.147 --> 00:02:41.867
♪ Quicker than a dart, make it into art

00:02:41.947 --> 00:02:42.947
♪ Bump-bump

00:02:43.027 --> 00:02:44.347
♪ That's the way it's done,
it's a lot of fun

00:02:44.427 --> 00:02:45.387
♪ Bump-bump

00:02:45.547 --> 00:02:47.907
♪ Liftin' my funk,
makin' sculpture outta junk ♪

00:02:48.307 --> 00:02:49.827
-(CHUCKLES)
-(DEVICE BEEPING)

00:02:49.987 --> 00:02:52.427
What's that? (SCOFFS) There we go!

00:02:52.507 --> 00:02:53.187
Somebody's interrupting genius!

00:02:55.387 --> 00:02:58.067
-(GASPS) Well, hey, there, buddy!
-(CHUCKLES) Mater!

00:02:58.147 --> 00:02:59.907
You know, I was just thinking of you

00:02:59.947 --> 00:03:01.627
and here you are lookin' right at me!

00:03:01.787 --> 00:03:05.587
You see me okay? Hang on a second
there. Hold on. Let me see here.

00:03:06.867 --> 00:03:08.107
-That better?
-(CHUCKLES)

00:03:08.627 --> 00:03:10.947
Looking you straight
in the eye there, pal.

00:03:10.987 --> 00:03:13.347
Hey, sorry about calling so late.

00:03:14.027 --> 00:03:15.147
Shoot, not for me it's not.

00:03:15.227 --> 00:03:17.107
I'm always burning that midnight oil.

00:03:17.267 --> 00:03:19.387
So get me caught up on everything.

00:03:19.627 --> 00:03:21.387
Well, actually kind of hoping

00:03:21.467 --> 00:03:22.987
I might hear what's going on back home.

00:03:23.147 --> 00:03:26.387
Not much. If you don't
count Sarge and Fillmore

00:03:26.467 --> 00:03:27.707
tryin' to run the tire shop.

00:03:27.907 --> 00:03:31.227
But tell Luigi not to worry,
Sarge is gonna track down...

00:03:31.387 --> 00:03:33.827
every last tire
that Fillmore done gived away.

00:03:34.587 --> 00:03:36.587
Other than that, everything's good.

00:03:36.667 --> 00:03:38.307
-How's Sally?
-Oh, she's fine.

00:03:38.907 --> 00:03:41.147
Keeping busy at the Cone.
She misses you.

00:03:41.307 --> 00:03:44.027
Well, shoot! We all do
when you're on the road.

00:03:45.267 --> 00:03:49.547
Yeah. You know, I've been
kind of thinking about that.

00:03:49.707 --> 00:03:51.627
You know, what we should do

00:03:51.667 --> 00:03:52.987
when I'm not on the road anymore.

00:03:53.667 --> 00:03:55.067
What do you mean not on the road?

00:03:55.987 --> 00:03:57.947
Well, you know.

00:03:59.187 --> 00:04:00.867
Mater, I can't do this forever.

00:04:01.627 --> 00:04:02.627
Huh?

00:04:04.027 --> 00:04:06.827
I'm just not getting anywhere
with the training.

00:04:07.027 --> 00:04:09.227
If anything,
I've gotten slower not faster.

00:04:09.907 --> 00:04:11.787
Shoot, buddy, it'll work out.

00:04:11.867 --> 00:04:13.107
Just tell me what the problem is...

00:04:13.267 --> 00:04:15.467
and I'll stay right here
with you until we fix it.

00:04:16.107 --> 00:04:18.307
That's just it, Mater. I don't know.

00:04:19.107 --> 00:04:21.027
And I feel like I'm all out of ideas.

00:04:21.787 --> 00:04:23.027
Hmm.

00:04:23.067 --> 00:04:26.147
All right, let me think.
Oh! You know what I'd do?

00:04:26.347 --> 00:04:27.547
What?

00:04:29.187 --> 00:04:31.227
I don't know. I got nothin'.

00:04:31.547 --> 00:04:33.467
I guess I ain't Doc when it comes to that.

00:04:34.867 --> 00:04:37.787
I would give anything
to talk to him right now.

00:04:37.947 --> 00:04:40.587
Yep, there was nobody
smarter than old Doc.

00:04:40.747 --> 00:04:42.467
Well, except for maybe
whoever taught him.

00:04:42.667 --> 00:04:44.907
Yeah. Wait. What?

00:04:45.507 --> 00:04:47.507
Everybody was taught
by somebody, right?

00:04:47.547 --> 00:04:48.667
Take my cousin Doyle.

00:04:49.187 --> 00:04:51.387
He taught me how to sing
and whistle at the same time.

00:04:51.547 --> 00:04:52.987
He was very musical that way.

00:04:53.147 --> 00:04:56.147
Smokey. Mater, you're brilliant.

00:04:56.387 --> 00:04:59.707
Ah, well... It's all about
the shape of your teeth.

00:04:59.867 --> 00:05:01.187
I got to go to Thomasville.

00:05:01.347 --> 00:05:02.667
MATER: Oh, well, good.

00:05:02.747 --> 00:05:05.147
You know me, buddy,
I'm always happy to help.

00:05:05.307 --> 00:05:09.067
Think I am better at that than most folks.
You know, talkin' and stuff.

00:05:16.107 --> 00:05:17.507
(MACK HONKING)

00:05:24.827 --> 00:05:25.827
Hey, Cruz.

00:05:26.507 --> 00:05:28.267
You won't talk me out of this,
Mr. McQueen.

00:05:28.427 --> 00:05:30.907
I'm going back. I resign as your trainer.

00:05:31.547 --> 00:05:35.427
All right. I accept your resignation. Bye.

00:05:36.187 --> 00:05:38.027
Oh... Okay.

00:05:38.867 --> 00:05:42.627
But since you cleared your calendar,
why don't you come with us?

00:05:42.787 --> 00:05:44.827
I'm looking for someone named Smokey.

00:05:44.987 --> 00:05:48.307
Hoping he can help me.
Maybe he can help you too.

00:05:48.827 --> 00:05:49.827
Nah.

00:05:49.987 --> 00:05:53.147
Come on. I fixed it.

00:05:54.347 --> 00:05:56.707
No. Thanks anyway. But I'm done.

00:05:57.147 --> 00:06:01.427
Okay. But maybe this will
change your mind. Hit it.

00:06:01.627 --> 00:06:02.627
(UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING)

00:06:03.067 --> 00:06:05.667
First I'm going to loosen up
these ancient joints--

00:06:05.827 --> 00:06:07.227
No, please don't.

00:06:07.307 --> 00:06:08.907
I'm sorry. I'm sorry.

00:06:09.107 --> 00:06:10.947
I'm sorry that I yelled.

00:06:10.987 --> 00:06:14.387
It wasn't your fault
that I almost got killed.

00:06:14.467 --> 00:06:17.707
But now you're leaving
and you won't get on the ramp.

00:06:17.907 --> 00:06:19.107
-CRUZ: All right, I'll go.
-You won't get on the ramp.

00:06:19.187 --> 00:06:20.187
All right, I'll go! Just stop!

00:06:25.827 --> 00:06:27.587
CRUZ: How do you know
Smokey's going to be here?

00:06:27.747 --> 00:06:29.067
McQUEEN: I don't.

00:06:29.467 --> 00:06:32.347
CRUZ: Oh. Do you know
if he's even alive?

00:06:32.987 --> 00:06:33.987
McQUEEN: Nope.

00:06:34.667 --> 00:06:35.707
CRUZ: Okay.

00:06:37.027 --> 00:06:39.787
So tell me this: how do you know
if it's Smokey? Is there such--

00:06:39.947 --> 00:06:42.107
McQUEEN: Wait. Mack, pull over!

00:06:42.267 --> 00:06:43.627
Back it up! Back it up.

00:07:01.107 --> 00:07:02.587
McQUEEN: Good to see you, Doc.

00:07:03.067 --> 00:07:05.827
Hey, isn't that your old crew chief?

00:07:06.667 --> 00:07:09.907
Hey, Cruz? You want to
check out the home track

00:07:10.027 --> 00:07:11.787
of the greatest racer ever?

00:07:14.347 --> 00:07:17.227
Aren't we supposed to be
looking for Smokey?

00:07:17.347 --> 00:07:19.347
Oh, that's right, he's dead.

00:07:19.507 --> 00:07:21.307
McQUEEN: We don't know that.

00:07:29.427 --> 00:07:31.387
Are you sure you have time for this?

00:07:32.267 --> 00:07:34.947
For this, I do.

